            "review_title": "Review at Manten",
            "review_text": "ying g\n1 contribution\n0\nNo welcome, no thank you, a disappointing shop\nOct 2025 • Solo\nNo welcome, no thank you, no lousy shop\n\nI used it every time I came to Hanoi.\nI like the atmosphere of the restaurant where I can eat calmly by myself, and I also like the acid boiled noodles here, so I came to look forward to it this time, but the level of customer service dropped considerably.\nWhen I entered, there was no greeting, and although one of the staff noticed me and greeted me, I sat down and no one came to pick up my order. I called the clerk and he was right in front of me. He doesn't even come out and he doesn't want to do it.\nEven after that, there was no \"yes\" when I ordered it, so I didn't know if it was being conveyed, so I didn't mind urging it.\nI'm not saying that it's being done by a Japanese owner, so it's either not being managed or being licked.\n\nIt's very disappointing because this restaurant didn't serve customers at such a low level, I can see why there are no customers today, this is not the case.\nEven if it tastes good, it won't come again.\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten October 7, 2025",
